#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536935} :activity/id #uuid "dc0e234d-b992-588f-b6af-c684a6467dfa" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536931 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "381464a8-f1f7-542d-a442-763dabbf0722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330448} {:answer/id #uuid "52ccb450-b1ee-5c92-99d3-724f5548b247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330702} {:answer/id #uuid "831193f3-07ba-55f2-8e65-22822c9ce5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331112} {:answer/id #uuid "9f76c378-2dc9-5123-ac6f-b8fd6a7ce8fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331385} {:answer/id #uuid "efb7e2c1-6247-5e8f-8d91-f3e2b9a5e8fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332054}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332054} :answer-field/id #uuid "51abc2de-d0da-5fce-aa24-dac010401f27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e19633c-fd26-592a-9173-f3506939c283" :question/math-academy-id "q-50233" :question/problem "$\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1))(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+D) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2D \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$"} :step/id #uuid "5e6cf617-c728-543e-ba88-85418d553d8f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536973}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536935 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ada2e3d-0769-5b5a-85e6-218cbeec1c89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536348} {:answer/id #uuid "4b33b710-8754-5317-ad8d-edc5c3f9305d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536402} {:answer/id #uuid "725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536473} {:answer/id #uuid "cc05201a-8232-5a04-8ce3-e3ac354a9f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536605} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4553a-62e1-59c9-8854-5587cc1e9c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536680}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536473} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6fa46cf-d1f0-5fd4-a76c-c62db6438a9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "50970995-9b99-52ed-ae6b-c20b930d578c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9537" :question/problem "![](images/50/5034bb902aadd151cc1a28764e054dbdd6a694ad653f50557e5fc208c8ec2342.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above).\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing $x=\\theta $ in the above identity, the integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={2\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6658199f-07f8-5ee5-96c7-e1415acede8a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536931}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536957 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26347220-3d03-59ee-8e7b-cb61d02c8618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536341} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce04388-54d1-53d5-91e9-530b14e04a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-7}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536379} {:answer/id #uuid "58346a39-6f7b-5629-aba6-151206e88d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-7}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536441} {:answer/id #uuid "d82f7750-cdb5-5af6-a415-d4526008d845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536624} {:answer/id #uuid "e52ce18d-55d4-5980-93b5-05d516aca7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-5}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536645} :answer-field/id #uuid "2122b91f-e6b1-53a7-bc39-72f4271ba65f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49aa78c4-2d01-5b28-b29f-36722ae18536" :question/math-academy-id "q-109424" :question/problem "![](images/58/5806f57e41eeb5548b0c041533adf3952dd7f35236121f9056c57f03c2854ddc.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $y=\\sqrt{1-x}$ that lies in the first quadrant between $x=0$ and its $x$-intercept. What integral gives the area of the surface generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-x} & =0 \\\\ 1-x & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{1-x})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-x}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4(1-x)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{5-4x}{4(1-x)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-5}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a792d8fe-f954-5743-ab0d-63ffa1aac63c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536958}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536958 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd93bd0-5caf-5cdf-9fec-3bc7b09fd51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.3P(50\\,000\\,000+P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250663} {:answer/id #uuid "1f021ce1-6e5b-56e4-ba92-6b150b40127b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=50\\,000\\,000P(0.3+P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250816} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d57bd8-e7b5-52b2-aa74-d3c445be8ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.3P(50\\,000\\,000-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251947} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b8f5ab-73ab-512f-b3cc-a7df929a3e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=-0.3P(50\\,000\\,000-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252171} {:answer/id #uuid "ee065c7b-b94e-5f3b-a32b-5b87650db484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=50\\,000\\,000P(0.3-P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251947} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6690fcb-b915-5e44-8c44-d66de9e23524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "69d6c7c8-a17d-5595-94e0-1820b1ec12de" :question/math-academy-id "q-119290" :question/problem "A population of $50\\,000\\,000$ people is being vaccinated against a disease. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ vaccinated is jointly proportional to the number of people who have been vaccinated at time $t,$ measured in months, and the number of unvaccinated people. If the constant of proportionality is $0.3,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the growth rate of vaccinated people is *jointly* proportional to the number of people who have been vaccinated at time $t,$ and the number of unvaccinated people, the number of vaccinated people follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.3,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=50\\,000\\,000.$ Therefore, the number of people who have been vaccinated is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.3P(50\\,000\\,000-P).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a82d7e6d-d029-58a5-adca-46793e317249"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536973 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df50d26b-36b0-56c5-b8ab-6313ce61f333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1446" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536629}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536629} :answer-field/id #uuid "a36923dd-8b5c-56f5-b238-c554200e0681" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15462584-19cb-5b6e-9995-3d3c0d41935d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536317} :answer-field/id #uuid "b20711af-5c25-5a71-ae61-9921ee570e17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d80dc7c0-9327-55d2-9040-e9261d08f05c" :question/math-academy-id "q-349991" :question/problem "The total amount of money $M(t)$ in a charity’s fundraising account $t$ days after the first day of a campaign is given by the function\n\n$$\nM(t)=1500+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $M$ is measured in dollars, and $t\\ge 0$ is the time (in days) since the first day of the campaign.\n\nFind the time when the total amount is minimum, and how much money was in the account at that time.\n\nThe minimum amount is\n$$$\n{{field-1}}\nafter \n{{field-2}} days." :question/worked-solution "To find when the total amount is a minimum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1500+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1500)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=0$:\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}-27=0\\,⇒\\,t=3\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=3.$ To find out how much money is in the account when $t=3,$ we figure out $M(3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(3) & =1500+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1500+[{x}^{3}-27x]{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1500+[({3}^{3}-27(3))-(0)] \\\\  & =1500+[27-81] \\\\  & =1500-54 \\\\  & =1446\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1446<1500$, we conclude that the minimum amount is $$\\,1446$, and this will happen after $3$ days."} :step/id #uuid "d912ee93-2c60-59a8-8030-8b4cb9171afe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536957}}] :activity/title "Quiz 2" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536282}]}
